WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.800
In the new coordinates, Z
to the fourth equals one.

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.240
Only the four powers one, Z, Z
squared, and Z cubed are needed.

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:12.153
Every term of our sign polynomial
has the form h sub a b,

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:15.320
times Z to the a, times P to the b.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.400
The first index runs from zero to three;

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:21.240
the second from zero
to u squared minus one.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.300
Group the terms according
to their power of Z.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:29.620
Follow the coefficient and its
power of P as they move together.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.080
The terms with no Z go
into the first group.

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:38.380
Those with Z, Z squared, and Z cubed
go into the other three groups.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:40.800
We are showing representative terms;

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:45.220
the omitted powers of P continue
in exactly the same way.

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:51.360
For each a, call the polynomial
inside its group H sub a of P.

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:55.600
It is the sum of h sub
a b times P to the b,

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:58.360
over all u squared coefficient positions.

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:03.140
Keeping the common power
of Z outside gives h of Z

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:08.500
and P equals H zero of
P, plus Z H one of P,

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:14.520
plus Z squared H two of P,
plus Z cubed H three of P.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:17.160
Why is this expression unique?

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:22.420
The monomials Z to the a times P to the
b form the integer group-ring basis.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:26.820
Every basis position already
has its own sign coefficient.

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:31.680
Re-expand one group: the very
same coefficients are still there.

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:35.720
We have regrouped terms, without
adding different coefficients together.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:39.400
Each H sub a therefore still
has u squared coefficients,

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:44.360
all plus or minus one. No norm identity
was needed for this regrouping.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:47.420
In the guiding order thirty-six case,

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:51.840
u is three, so each H sub a
has nine coefficient positions.

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:56.220
Keep these entries symbolic; this
is not a constructed Hadamard row.

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:59.240
Choose a single power,
say P to the fourth.

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:03.140
The four signs h zero four, h one four,

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:06.600
h two four, and h three
four line up in one column.

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:10.200
These are the signs that will
combine when we evaluate Z.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:15.620
We now have the four-polynomial expression
ready for two independent checks.

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:19.040
Substituting fourth roots
for Z will preserve the

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:22.220
norm identity. Checking sums and
differences of the four signs

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:25.500
will explain why division by two
keeps the coefficients integral.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:29.880
Evaluation and parity will then come
together in the normalization step.
